    \item She falls behind 3 spots, so she is now in $4 + 3 = 7$th place.
    \item She jumps ahead 1 spot, so she is now in $7 - 1 = 6$th place.
\end{itemize}
Therefore, Finley finished the race in 6th place.

\textbf{Reasoning:}
Finley started in 1st place.
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Losing 5 spots: $1 - 5 = -4$. Since places are positive, we interpret "falling back" as moving to a higher place number, so we add 5 to her position: $1 + 5 = 6$.
    \item Moving ahead 2 spots: $6 - 2 = 4$.
    \item Falling behind 3 spots: $4 + 3 = 7$.
    \item Jumping ahead 1 spot: $7 - 1 = 6$.
\end{enumerate}

She finished in 6th place.

